      "source": [
        "The KNN fit is piecewise constant. The Gaussian kernel fit changes smoothly because the weights change smoothly as the target point moves.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Kernel Functions\n",
        "\n",
        "A kernel function is a nonnegative function that gives larger values to points near zero. For density estimation, we usually require\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "K(u)\\ge 0,\n",
        "\\qquad\n",
        "\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty}K(u)\\,du=1.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The scaled kernel is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "K_h(x,x_i)\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\frac{1}{h}\n",
        "K\\left(\\frac{x-x_i}{h}\\right).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The bandwidth $h$ controls how wide the kernel is.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Common Kernels\n",
        "\n",
        "The Gaussian kernel is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "K(u)\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\pi}}\n",
        "\\exp\\left(-\\frac{u^2}{2}\\right).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The uniform kernel is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "K(u)\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\frac{1}{2}I(|u|\\le 1).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The Epanechnikov kernel is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "K(u)\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\frac{3}{4}(1-u^2)I(|u|\\le 1).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The exact kernel shape is usually less important than the bandwidth. The bandwidth controls the main bias-variance tradeoff."
      ],
