        "### Local Averaging at One Target Point\n",
        "\n",
        "At a target point $x_0$, observations closer to $x_0$ receive larger kernel weights. For example, with a Gaussian kernel and bandwidth $h=0.5$,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "K_h(x_0,x_i)\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\frac{1}{h\\sqrt{2\\pi}}\n",
        "\\exp\\left\\{\n",
        "-\\frac{(x_0-x_i)^2}{2h^2}\n",
        "\\right\\}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The Nadaraya-Watson estimate at $x_0$ is the weighted average\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\hat f(x_0)\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\frac{\\sum_i K_h(x_0,x_i)y_i}{\\sum_i K_h(x_0,x_i)}.\n",
        "$$"
      ],
      "id": "4c9abd3d"
    },
