    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Small bandwidths can chase noise. Large bandwidths can oversmooth the curve.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Choosing the Bandwidth\n",
        "\n",
        "The bandwidth can be chosen by cross-validation. For regression, one simple method is to split the data, fit the smoother on the training part, and choose the bandwidth with the smallest validation mean squared error.\n",
        "\n",
        "For one-dimensional smoothing, a common rule-of-thumb bandwidth is Silverman's rule:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "h\n",
        "=\n",
        "1.06\\,\\hat\\sigma_x\\,n^{-1/5}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "This formula is useful as a starting value, but it depends on assumptions that may not hold in practice. Cross-validation is usually safer when prediction performance matters."
      ],
      "id": "6d1ba6aa"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "silverman_h = 1.06 * np.std(X, ddof=1) * len(X) ** (-1 / 5)\n",
        "silverman_h"
      ],
      "id": "fe719fb5",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The following code uses `GridSearchCV` with a small custom estimator. This keeps the bandwidth selection in the usual `sklearn` workflow."
      ],
      "id": "7c8d061c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.base import BaseEstimator, RegressorMixin\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import GridSearchCV\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import mean_squared_error\n",
        "\n",
        "class NadarayaWatsonRegressor(BaseEstimator, RegressorMixin):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, bandwidth=1.0):\n",
        "        self.bandwidth = bandwidth\n",
        "\n",
        "    def fit(self, X, y):\n",
        "        self.X_train_ = np.asarray(X).reshape(-1, 1)\n",
        "        self.y_train_ = np.asarray(y)\n",
        "        return self\n",
        "\n",
        "    def predict(self, X):\n",
        "        X = np.asarray(X).reshape(-1, 1)\n",
        "        distances = X - self.X_train_.T\n",
        "        weights = np.exp(-0.5 * (distances / self.bandwidth) ** 2)\n",
        "        weights = weights / weights.sum(axis=1, keepdims=True)\n",
        "        return weights @ self.y_train_\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "bandwidth_grid = {\n",
        "    \"bandwidth\": np.linspace(0.1, 1.2, 23),\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "grid = GridSearchCV(\n",
        "    NadarayaWatsonRegressor(),\n",
        "    param_grid=bandwidth_grid,\n",
        "    cv=5,\n",
        "    scoring=\"neg_mean_squared_error\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "grid.fit(X.reshape(-1, 1), y)\n",
        "\n",
        "grid.best_params_"
      ],
