      "source": [
        "## Local Linear Regression\n",
        "\n",
        "The Nadaraya-Watson estimator is a local constant estimator. Around each target point $x_0$, it fits a constant by weighted least squares.\n",
        "\n",
        "Local linear regression fits a line near each target point:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\min_{\\beta_0,\\beta_1}\n",
        "\\sum_{i=1}^n\n",
        "K_h(x_0,x_i)\n",
        "\\left[\n",
        "y_i-\\beta_0-\\beta_1(x_i-x_0)\n",
        "\\right]^2.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The fitted value at $x_0$ is the fitted intercept:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\hat f(x_0)=\\hat\\beta_0.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Local linear regression often improves boundary behavior. Near the edge of the data, a local average can be biased because there are observations on only one side of the target point. A local line can adjust for the slope.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-note}\n",
        "## Boundary bias\n",
        "\n",
        "Local averaging can be biased near the boundary of the data.\n",
        "\n",
        "Local linear regression reduces this problem by fitting a local trend instead of a local constant.\n",
        ":::"
      ],
      "id": "5f611f66"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "def local_linear_predict(X_train, y_train, X_new, bandwidth):\n",
        "    X_train = np.asarray(X_train)\n",
        "    y_train = np.asarray(y_train)\n",
        "    preds = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    for x0 in X_new:\n",
        "        z = X_train - x0\n",
        "        weights = np.exp(-0.5 * (z / bandwidth) ** 2)\n",
        "        design = np.column_stack([np.ones_like(z), z])\n",
        "        weighted_design = design * weights[:, None]\n",
        "        beta = np.linalg.pinv(weighted_design.T @ design) @ weighted_design.T @ y_train\n",
        "        preds.append(beta[0])\n",
        "\n",
        "    return np.asarray(preds)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "y_local_constant = kernel_regression_predict(X, y, X_grid, bandwidth=0.4)\n",
        "y_local_linear = local_linear_predict(X, y, X_grid, bandwidth=0.4)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.scatter(X, y, s=35, facecolors=\"none\", edgecolors=\"black\")\n",
        "plt.plot(X_grid, 2 * np.sin(X_grid), color=\"C0\", label=\"true function\")\n",
        "plt.plot(X_grid, y_local_constant, color=\"C1\", label=\"local constant\")\n",
        "plt.plot(X_grid, y_local_linear, color=\"C3\", label=\"local linear\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"x\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"y\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Local Constant versus Local Linear Smoothing\")\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "14a86fee",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Local Polynomial Regression\n",
        "\n",
        "Local linear regression can be extended to local polynomial regression. At each target point $x_0$, fit\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\min_{\\beta_0,\\ldots,\\beta_d}\n",
        "\\sum_{i=1}^n\n",
        "K_h(x_0,x_i)\n",
        "\\left[\n",
        "y_i-\\beta_0-\\sum_{r=1}^d \\beta_r(x_i-x_0)^r\n",
        "\\right]^2.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Then\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\hat f(x_0)=\\hat\\beta_0.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The degree $d$ controls the local shape:\n",
        "\n",
        "- $d=0$: local constant regression,\n",
        "- $d=1$: local linear regression,\n",
        "- $d=2$: local quadratic regression.\n",
        "\n",
        "Higher-degree local polynomials can reduce bias, but they may also become unstable if the bandwidth is too small or the data are sparse.\n",
        "\n",
        "The following code compares local constant, local linear, and local quadratic smoothing."
      ],
      "id": "0c379ba8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "def local_polynomial_predict(X_train, y_train, X_new, bandwidth, degree):\n",
        "    X_train = np.asarray(X_train)\n",
        "    y_train = np.asarray(y_train)\n",
        "    preds = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    for x0 in X_new:\n",
        "        z = X_train - x0\n",
        "        weights = np.exp(-0.5 * (z / bandwidth) ** 2)\n",
        "        design = np.column_stack([z**d for d in range(degree + 1)])\n",
        "        weighted_design = design * weights[:, None]\n",
        "        beta = np.linalg.pinv(weighted_design.T @ design) @ weighted_design.T @ y_train\n",
        "        preds.append(beta[0])\n",
        "\n",
        "    return np.asarray(preds)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "h_rule = silverman_h\n",
        "y_constant = kernel_regression_predict(X, y, X_grid, bandwidth=h_rule)\n",
        "y_linear = local_polynomial_predict(X, y, X_grid, bandwidth=h_rule, degree=1)\n",
        "y_quadratic = local_polynomial_predict(X, y, X_grid, bandwidth=h_rule, degree=2)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.scatter(X, y, s=30, facecolors=\"none\", edgecolors=\"black\")\n",
        "plt.plot(X_grid, 2 * np.sin(X_grid), color=\"C0\", label=\"true function\")\n",
        "plt.plot(X_grid, y_constant, color=\"C1\", label=\"local constant\")\n",
        "plt.plot(X_grid, y_linear, color=\"C3\", label=\"local linear\")\n",
        "plt.plot(X_grid, y_quadratic, color=\"C2\", label=\"local quadratic\")\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"x\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"y\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Local Polynomial Regression\")\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "d5ed3b19",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
